Root cause fixed in:

`firmware/libopencm3-examples/examples/stm32/f4/stm32f4-discovery/miniblink/miniblink.c`

### Root cause
The GPIOD peripheral clock enable call was missing from `gpio_setup()`.  
Without enabling `RCC_GPIOD`, writes to `GPIOD` configuration/output registers have no effect, so LED pin PD12 never toggles and the on-board LED stays off permanently.

### Fix applied
Reintroduced the clock enable line before GPIO configuration:

```c
rcc_periph_clock_enable(RCC_GPIOD);
```

This restores proper GPIO initialization and allows PD12 to toggle as intended.
